Package: epiLabR
Type: Package
Title: Educational Framework for Compartmental Epidemiological Modelling
Version: 0.3.0
Author: Vicente Castellar [aut, cre]
Authors@R:
    person("Vicente", "Castellar",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "vic.sebastia@gmail.com")
Description: Tools for simulating deterministic compartmental epidemiological
    models defined by systems of ordinary differential equations (ODEs). The
    package allows users to define custom epidemic models, simulate state
    trajectories over time, and explore model behavior under different
    parameter settings. It includes implementations of classical
    susceptible-infectious-recovered (SIR) models and related extensions.
    An optional 'shiny' application is provided for interactive visualization
    and exploration of epidemic scenarios. The methodological framework is
    informed by Anderson and May (1991, ISBN:9780198540403),
    Hethcote (2000, <doi:10.1137/S0036144500371907>), and Keeling and Rohani
    (2008, <doi:10.1515/9781400841035>).
